

BSC‑01 DESIGN WHITE SHEET

Sovereign Cognitive Silicon — Architectural Definition

1. System Identity

Device Name: BSC‑01 (Sovereign Cognitive Silicon)Classification: Autonomous Edge Cognition SubstrateDesign Intent:A self‑contained computational organism capable of sensing, modeling, adapting to, and surviving within its physical environment through decentralized reflex loops, hierarchical policy engines, and a cryptographically sovereign core.

2. System Boundary

The BSC‑01 operates as a closed cognitive substrate.No external agent — host, network, or supervisory controller — may access or modify:

internal cognition state

field simulation buffers

decrypted telemetry

strategic decision pathways

All external interaction occurs through summary‑only interfaces and policy‑bounded control vectors.

3. Architectural Pillars

Decentralized Cognition Array

A distributed mesh of reflex microcores (Sucker Nodes) organized under Arm‑level policy engines, enabling real‑time environmental response.

Environment Field Engine

A hardware diffusion solver maintaining a continuous chemical‑field representation of the environment, updated every global tick.

Core Brain Tile

A global strategic classifier that evaluates Arm summaries and emits the Global Policy Vector (GPV) governing system‑wide behavior.

Crypto Vault Engine + TLU

A sealed cryptographic enclave responsible for encrypting, authenticating, and immutably storing all strategic transitions and fault events.

Host Interface Bridge

A filtered command surface enforcing sovereign boundaries and preventing unauthorized introspection.

4. Core Runtime Loop

Field Update:EFE computes next‑state chemical field.

Reflex Sampling:Sucker Nodes sense local gradients and emit 32‑bit reflex packets.

Arm Aggregation:Arms compress thousands of reflex events into 64‑bit summaries.

Global Strategy:GSAC evaluates summaries and selects the active archetype.

Policy Broadcast:Core emits a 32‑bit GPV; Arms ACK/ERR; commit occurs atomically.

Ledger Append:All transitions are encrypted and appended to the on‑die ledger.

5. Sovereign Guarantees

No plaintext internal state ever leaves the die.

All cognition is autonomous and locally adaptive.

Host cannot override safety constraints or strategic decisions.

All critical events are immutably logged.

Panic and quarantine pathways ensure survival under fault.

6. Implementation Notes

Message Fabric and EFE crossbar co‑designed for minimal latency.

CVE/TLU enclave isolated in power, clock, and routing domains.

GPV commit line skew‑controlled for single‑cycle global synchronization.

All reflex loops guaranteed deterministic within one global tick.

